PR #269 - changes required
1. [BLOCKER] backend/openbot/runtime/providers.py:201-207 - `small_chat_model` only falls back when constructing the provider client raises `ValueError`/`RuntimeError`. The LangChain clients generally construct successfully even when the selected model is unavailable; the failure occurs later on `ainvoke`, and both title generation (`backend/openbot/runtime/renaming.py:52`) and memory reflection (`backend/openbot/runtime/memory.py:166-170`) invoke the returned model without any fallback. Thus an unavailable configured/default small model still fails the side task instead of retrying with the bot's main model, which is the central issue #255 requirement. Implement fallback around the side-task invocation (or an equivalent availability-validated factory) and add a regression test that makes the small model's invocation fail and verifies the main model is invoked.
2. [BLOCKER] backend/openbot/runtime/renaming.py:52 - this new path accesses `services.small_model_factory` directly, unlike `MemoryReflector.make_manager`, which uses `getattr`. Any existing lightweight service/test double exposing only `model_factory` now raises `AttributeError` before title generation, despite the PR's compatibility goal. Use the same optional-attribute fallback and add a title-generation test with a service double that has no `small_model_factory` attribute.

Validation: reviewed exact pushed head e4c20a32b9efeb56d6377811c3e037d762a33c83; changed-file diff covered all 10 files; current backend/frontend CI checks are green and PR is mergeable. I did not run the suite or linter per review instructions.

